1
00:00:01,921 --> 00:00:03,298
Hoo, hoo!

2
00:00:03,410 --> 00:00:04,337
Hi!

3
00:00:04,387 --> 00:00:06,415
It's me, Popcorn!

4
00:00:06,536 --> 00:00:11,767
Welcome to Popcorn Tales, the
cozy nest of bedtime stories.

5
00:00:12,079 --> 00:00:15,493
Hug your teddy, because
tonight's story is:

6
00:00:15,543 --> 00:00:18,586
The Three Little Pigs and the Brick House!

7
00:00:23,195 --> 00:00:28,784
Once upon a time, on top of a green
hill, there lived a very loving mother

8
00:00:28,834 --> 00:00:32,497
pig, in a stone house
with her three children.

9
00:00:33,138 --> 00:00:38,991
Nico was the most playful, Lalo was
the sleepiest, and Rosa was the most

10
00:00:39,041 --> 00:00:40,566
careful of the three.

11
00:00:41,212 --> 00:00:46,029
One sunny morning, the mother pig
called her children to the front door.

12
00:00:46,613 --> 00:00:50,510
My dears, it is time for each of
you to build a house of your own.

13
00:00:50,785 --> 00:00:55,017
Make it a strong house, because a
very hungry wolf lives in the woods,

14
00:00:55,067 --> 00:00:56,717
the mother pig said.

15
00:00:57,371 --> 00:01:00,146
Don't worry, Mom, we will be very careful,

16
00:01:00,196 --> 00:01:01,763
Nico promised.

17
00:01:02,414 --> 00:01:06,586
The three of them gave their mother
a big hug, picked up their bundles,

18
00:01:06,636 --> 00:01:08,522
and went down the hill singing.

19
00:01:11,430 --> 00:01:16,316
Popcorn the owl decided to follow
their journey from up in the sky.

20
00:01:16,945 --> 00:01:18,322
Hoo, hoo!

21
00:01:18,440 --> 00:01:21,900
Three pigs all alone
in the big wide world?

22
00:01:22,046 --> 00:01:24,558
I'm going to keep an eye on those three,

23
00:01:24,608 --> 00:01:26,133
Popcorn said.

24
00:01:27,231 --> 00:01:31,987
At the very first bend in the road,
Nico met a farmer with a cart full of

25
00:01:32,037 --> 00:01:33,353
golden straw.

26
00:01:34,009 --> 00:01:36,703
Mister farmer, could you please
give me some of that straw,

27
00:01:36,753 --> 00:01:38,114
so I can build my house?

28
00:01:38,164 --> 00:01:39,606
Nico asked.

29
00:01:40,270 --> 00:01:45,372
The farmer gave him a huge bundle of
straw, and Nico built his house in just

30
00:01:45,422 --> 00:01:46,622
one hour.

31
00:01:47,059 --> 00:01:47,830
Done!

32
00:01:47,880 --> 00:01:49,688
Now I have the whole afternoon to play,

33
00:01:49,738 --> 00:01:52,888
Nico said, rolling in the grass.

34
00:01:53,606 --> 00:01:57,923
Further along, Lalo got a big
pile of sticks from a woodcutter,

35
00:01:57,995 --> 00:02:01,695
tied them together with string, and
made a house that was a little bit

36
00:02:01,745 --> 00:02:02,945
sturdier.

37
00:02:03,408 --> 00:02:04,468
Done!

38
00:02:04,518 --> 00:02:06,691
Now I can take a nap in the shade,

39
00:02:06,741 --> 00:02:08,655
Lalo said, yawning.

40
00:02:09,294 --> 00:02:14,342
But Rosa walked on a bit further, until
she met a man with a cart full of red

41
00:02:14,392 --> 00:02:15,592
bricks.

42
00:02:15,992 --> 00:02:18,170
She worked all day long:

43
00:02:18,229 --> 00:02:22,393
she stacked the bricks one by
one, spread mortar between them,

44
00:02:22,452 --> 00:02:25,782
and even built a fireplace
with a tall chimney.

45
00:02:26,436 --> 00:02:28,225
Rosa, come and play with us!

46
00:02:28,441 --> 00:02:29,590
Why all that hard work?

47
00:02:29,640 --> 00:02:31,818
Nico shouted from the road.

48
00:02:32,442 --> 00:02:36,274
A well-built house takes longer,
but it truly keeps you safe,

49
00:02:36,324 --> 00:02:39,363
Rosa answered, wiping her forehead.

50
00:02:40,459 --> 00:02:44,381
Late that afternoon, a grey
wolf came out of the woods,

51
00:02:44,431 --> 00:02:48,220
with a long snout and a
tummy rumbling with hunger.

52
00:02:48,906 --> 00:02:52,626
He smelled pig, and went
straight to the straw house.

53
00:02:54,319 --> 00:02:57,308
Little pig, little pig, let me come in!

54
00:02:57,358 --> 00:03:00,133
the wolf said, knocking on the door.

55
00:03:00,761 --> 00:03:03,993
No, no, not by the hair
of my chinny chin chin!

56
00:03:04,043 --> 00:03:07,401
Nico answered, trembling behind the door.

57
00:03:07,903 --> 00:03:11,709
Then I'll huff, and I'll puff,
and I'll blow your house in!

58
00:03:11,759 --> 00:03:12,992
the wolf said.

59
00:03:13,639 --> 00:03:18,436
And the wolf puffed up his cheeks, and
he huffed and he puffed with all his

60
00:03:18,486 --> 00:03:19,686
might.

61
00:03:26,189 --> 00:03:31,125
The straw house flew up into the air,
like a pile of dry leaves on a windy

62
00:03:31,175 --> 00:03:32,375
day.

63
00:03:32,640 --> 00:03:34,596
But Nico was faster:

64
00:03:34,682 --> 00:03:39,077
he ran down the road without looking
back, all the way to his brother's house

65
00:03:39,127 --> 00:03:40,327
of sticks.

66
00:03:43,081 --> 00:03:43,941
Hoo!

67
00:03:43,991 --> 00:03:47,423
Run as fast as you can, Nico, run!

68
00:03:47,473 --> 00:03:49,762
Popcorn called from up above.

69
00:03:50,878 --> 00:03:55,092
Lalo woke up with his brother banging
on the door, and the two of them locked

70
00:03:55,142 --> 00:03:56,695
the door in a hurry.

71
00:03:57,344 --> 00:04:01,744
Soon after, the wolf
arrived, licking his snout.

72
00:04:03,355 --> 00:04:06,406
Little pigs, little pigs, let me come in!

73
00:04:06,456 --> 00:04:07,689
the wolf said.

74
00:04:08,299 --> 00:04:12,031
No, no, not by the hair
of our chinny chin chins!

75
00:04:12,081 --> 00:04:13,620
Lalo answered.

76
00:04:14,161 --> 00:04:17,967
Then I'll huff, and I'll puff,
and I'll blow your house in!

77
00:04:18,017 --> 00:04:19,250
the wolf said.

78
00:04:19,925 --> 00:04:24,222
The wolf huffed and he puffed,
and he puffed and he huffed,

79
00:04:24,272 --> 00:04:28,853
until the whole house fell apart, and
the branches rolled across the ground.

80
00:04:35,744 --> 00:04:40,180
The two brothers ran off hand in hand,
and didn't stop until they reached the

81
00:04:40,230 --> 00:04:42,602
door of Rosa's brick house.

82
00:04:45,501 --> 00:04:46,417
Rosa!

83
00:04:46,467 --> 00:04:47,387
Rosa!

84
00:04:47,437 --> 00:04:50,085
Open the door, the wolf
is coming after us!

85
00:04:50,135 --> 00:04:51,618
Nico shouted.

86
00:04:52,701 --> 00:04:58,101
Rosa opened the door, her brothers rushed
inside, and she slid the bolt shut,

87
00:04:58,160 --> 00:04:59,587
nice and tight.

88
00:05:02,914 --> 00:05:06,787
The wolf arrived right after,
tired from all that running.

89
00:05:08,411 --> 00:05:11,462
Little pigs, little pigs, let me come in!

90
00:05:11,512 --> 00:05:12,745
the wolf said.

91
00:05:13,372 --> 00:05:16,744
No, no, not by the hair
of my chinny chin chin!

92
00:05:16,794 --> 00:05:19,805
Rosa answered, in a calm voice.

93
00:05:20,340 --> 00:05:24,146
Then I'll huff, and I'll puff,
and I'll blow your house in!

94
00:05:24,196 --> 00:05:25,429
the wolf said.

95
00:05:26,082 --> 00:05:28,398
The wolf huffed and he puffed.

96
00:05:28,608 --> 00:05:30,870
He puffed and he huffed.

97
00:05:31,061 --> 00:05:33,877
And he huffed and he puffed one more time.

98
00:05:40,744 --> 00:05:44,638
But the brick house didn't move at
all, and not a single brick fell out of

99
00:05:44,688 --> 00:05:45,888
place.

100
00:05:46,286 --> 00:05:47,662
Hoo, hoo!

101
00:05:47,750 --> 00:05:52,943
That house was built with care,
Mister Wolf, there's no use blowing,

102
00:05:52,993 --> 00:05:55,199
Popcorn laughed from the roof.

103
00:05:55,809 --> 00:05:57,634
Sorry, Rosa.

104
00:05:57,775 --> 00:06:00,415
You were right, work
done well is worth it,

105
00:06:00,465 --> 00:06:01,754
Lalo said.

106
00:06:02,848 --> 00:06:07,942
But the wolf was stubborn, and decided
to use his wits instead of his breath.

107
00:06:08,471 --> 00:06:11,969
Rosa, I know a field full
of delicious turnips.

108
00:06:12,190 --> 00:06:16,694
Tomorrow, at six in the morning,
I'll come by so we can go together,

109
00:06:16,744 --> 00:06:20,255
the wolf said, in the
sweetest voice in the world.

110
00:06:20,894 --> 00:06:24,621
Rosa thought for a moment,
and answered with a smile:

111
00:06:24,671 --> 00:06:28,544
How lovely, Mister Wolf,
tomorrow at six I'll be ready.

112
00:06:29,191 --> 00:06:33,641
But Rosa woke up at five, went
to the field all by herself,

113
00:06:33,691 --> 00:06:38,507
filled her basket with turnips, and
came back home before the sun came up.

114
00:06:41,043 --> 00:06:46,590
When the wolf arrived, at six o'clock
sharp, Rosa was already cooking a turnip

115
00:06:46,640 --> 00:06:49,054
soup that smelled wonderful.

116
00:06:49,575 --> 00:06:53,503
Rosa, I also know an apple
tree full of red apples.

117
00:06:53,718 --> 00:06:56,801
Tomorrow, at five, I'll come by,

118
00:06:56,851 --> 00:06:58,085
the wolf said.

119
00:06:58,741 --> 00:07:03,775
This time, Rosa woke up at four,
but the apple tree was far away,

120
00:07:03,825 --> 00:07:07,178
and while she was up in the
branches, picking apples,

121
00:07:07,228 --> 00:07:08,780
the wolf showed up.

122
00:07:09,341 --> 00:07:11,508
Good morning, Mister Wolf!

123
00:07:11,620 --> 00:07:13,975
Catch this apple, it's delicious,

124
00:07:14,025 --> 00:07:18,730
Rosa said, and threw an apple
far away, down the hill.

125
00:07:19,352 --> 00:07:24,135
While the wolf ran after the apple,
Rosa jumped down from the tree,

126
00:07:24,185 --> 00:07:26,627
and ran home with her basket full.

127
00:07:29,962 --> 00:07:32,973
The next day, the wolf showed up again.

128
00:07:33,518 --> 00:07:37,141
Rosa, there's a fair on top
of the hill this afternoon.

129
00:07:37,350 --> 00:07:40,390
I'll come by at three,
so we can go together,

130
00:07:40,440 --> 00:07:41,674
the wolf said.

131
00:07:42,324 --> 00:07:46,524
Rosa went to the fair at two,
and bought a wooden butter churn,

132
00:07:46,574 --> 00:07:48,919
tall and round like a barrel.

133
00:07:49,576 --> 00:07:53,407
On her way back, she saw
the wolf coming up the hill,

134
00:07:53,479 --> 00:07:54,893
straight toward her!

135
00:07:55,517 --> 00:07:59,537
Quick as lightning, Rosa
hid inside the butter churn,

136
00:07:59,587 --> 00:08:01,209
and closed the lid.

137
00:08:01,829 --> 00:08:05,812
But the churn tipped over, and
began to roll down the hill,

138
00:08:06,023 --> 00:08:10,187
faster and faster, making
a tremendous noise.

139
00:08:11,907 --> 00:08:17,001
The wolf saw that big round thing
rolling, bouncing and rumbling toward him,

140
00:08:17,115 --> 00:08:19,793
and he got the biggest fright of his life.

141
00:08:20,368 --> 00:08:21,428
Help!

142
00:08:21,478 --> 00:08:22,919
A wooden monster!

143
00:08:22,969 --> 00:08:28,480
the wolf shouted, and ran off into the
woods, with his tail between his legs.

144
00:08:29,061 --> 00:08:30,438
Hoo, hoo!

145
00:08:30,541 --> 00:08:31,813
What a ride!

146
00:08:31,921 --> 00:08:35,261
That pig is the cleverest
one in the countryside,

147
00:08:35,311 --> 00:08:40,822
Popcorn said, laughing so hard
she almost fell off the stall.

148
00:08:41,790 --> 00:08:42,823
That's it!

149
00:08:42,873 --> 00:08:46,634
I'm going to climb onto the roof,
and come in through the chimney!

150
00:08:46,684 --> 00:08:47,918
the wolf said.

151
00:08:48,582 --> 00:08:50,572
Rosa wasn't scared at all:

152
00:08:50,622 --> 00:08:55,572
it was laundry day, and in the cold
fireplace there was a huge tub,

153
00:08:55,622 --> 00:08:58,355
full of cold water and soapy foam.

154
00:08:58,994 --> 00:09:02,763
Nico, Lalo, help me push the
tub right under the chimney,

155
00:09:02,813 --> 00:09:04,157
Rosa said.

156
00:09:04,786 --> 00:09:10,380
The wolf came down the chimney, slipped,
and landed right in the icy water!

157
00:09:12,551 --> 00:09:18,126
The wolf jumped out, soaking wet,
sneezing, and covered in foam from his head

158
00:09:18,176 --> 00:09:19,854
to the tip of his tail.

159
00:09:21,771 --> 00:09:22,902
Achoo!

160
00:09:22,952 --> 00:09:24,498
Not cold water!

161
00:09:24,548 --> 00:09:25,906
the wolf shouted.

162
00:09:26,573 --> 00:09:30,273
Rosa opened the door, and the
wolf ran off into the woods,

163
00:09:30,323 --> 00:09:33,265
and never bothered the
three siblings again.

164
00:09:33,947 --> 00:09:38,689
They say that, ever since that day, he
has learned to grow his own turnips,

165
00:09:38,739 --> 00:09:41,319
and never goes anywhere near a chimney.

166
00:09:41,960 --> 00:09:46,799
In the weeks that followed, Nico and
Lalo built their own brick houses,

167
00:09:46,849 --> 00:09:48,708
right next to Rosa's house.

168
00:09:49,348 --> 00:09:53,243
On the first Sunday, the mother
pig came to visit her children,

169
00:09:53,293 --> 00:09:56,859
and they all ate turnip
soup and apple pie together.

170
00:09:57,421 --> 00:09:59,137
I am so proud of you.

171
00:09:59,229 --> 00:10:03,291
A strong house is built with
patience, and so is a strong family,

172
00:10:03,341 --> 00:10:04,991
the mother pig said.

173
00:10:05,648 --> 00:10:10,917
And Popcorn, perched on a chimney,
blinked her big eyes and smiled,

174
00:10:10,967 --> 00:10:14,284
because she loved happy endings very much.

175
00:10:21,612 --> 00:10:22,812
The End.

176
00:10:24,527 --> 00:10:25,239
Hoo...

177
00:10:25,289 --> 00:10:26,313
Psst!

178
00:10:26,363 --> 00:10:27,935
Are you still awake?

179
00:10:28,089 --> 00:10:30,143
Did you like tonight's story?

180
00:10:30,253 --> 00:10:34,968
The three little pigs showed us that
work done with patience and care truly

181
00:10:35,018 --> 00:10:39,559
keeps us safe, and that cleverness
is worth more than strength.

182
00:10:39,873 --> 00:10:44,179
Good night, sleep tight, and
have the sweetest dreams.

183
00:10:44,475 --> 00:10:49,373
Grown-ups: if you enjoyed it,
please subscribe to Popcorn Tales,

184
00:10:49,423 --> 00:10:51,829
for more stories at bedtime.

185
00:10:52,132 --> 00:10:53,332
Hoo...

